(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["CanonicalHypergraph", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"8757aca7-3902-4c4c-a9ab-d0e5bd8ab57f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"CanonicalHypergraph", "[", "hg", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"f73862ad-2b32-fb47-ba78-1d0b093c68c0"],
 " ",
 "gives a canonical representative of the isomorphism class of hg."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"564c95cc-c668-cf4d-87ca-35d362078a0e"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"86a595f6-26f0-154c-80bf-a9c985b79c0f"],

Cell["\<\
The vertices of the result are renamed to 1, 2, ... and the labels are \
replaced by the placeholders \[FormalL][1], \[FormalL][2], ..., since labels \
count only up to renaming.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d075c273-9402-9a44-8dd7-a6bc2e897ad8"],

Cell["\<\
Two hypergraphs are isomorphic exactly when their canonical forms are \
identical.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"802150ed-fe9c-a149-887f-30849af1c20d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Labeled\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"5f82d702-7f9e-a540-abaf-f802c497e96d"],
 " the skeleton is canonicalized instead, and the result carries no labels at \
all."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"43b35868-5db5-5449-ad48-9acdf395d880"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The setting ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"e5bdb541-1127-154e-8d53-ce63857bc214"],
 " narrows the search by grouping vertices into classes that no isomorphism \
can mix up. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<BruteForce\>\""}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"03e08b80-bd6f-5a41-83a6-e51dcbc4ae2e"],
 " searches every ordering of the vertices instead, and exists to cross-check \
the default."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5aae7c76-79c8-9c47-9c2f-b49e67eb03a9"],

Cell["\<\
Both Method settings are functions of the isomorphism class alone, so they \
always agree about whether two hypergraphs are isomorphic, but they settle on \
different representatives of the same class. The two settings must therefore \
not be mixed within a single comparison.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e443548c-e39c-e845-892e-f03cd2082f93"],

Cell["\<\
The search is exhaustive. When it would exceed 40320 candidate orderings the \
message CanonicalHypergraph::large is produced and the computation proceeds.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0cc9e78e-7824-bd49-af74-23cde1b63b15"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"44bd4b67-4a36-d048-90ab-4a34dfa8e7a4"],

Cell["\<\
Two spellings of the same directed path have the same canonical form:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"4a213e85-293b-2a45-99e4-3ebaf213c561"],

Cell["\<\
a = Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}}];
b = Hypergraph[{{10, 20}, {20, 30}}];
{CanonicalHypergraph[a], CanonicalHypergraph[b]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"d621a01a-d323-2044-ac0b-9659a6aadc84"],

